WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.560
- Hi, I'm Natalia Dyer.

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:02.660
- Hi, I'm Charlie Heaton.

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:04.230
- And we're gonna break down a scene

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.530
shot-by-shot from
- From.

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.063
- Stranger Things Season 3.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:12.593
- Where is she?

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:15.143
- I don't know.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.821
- Are you sure this is the right room?

00:00:17.821 --> 00:00:19.228
(lights zapping)
- Yeah.

00:00:19.228 --> 00:00:20.240
(tense music)

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.293
- She's gone home.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:28.880
We were hoping it might come back.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.830
- We shot this over two, was it two days?

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:31.840
Two full days.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.840
12 to 14 hours, so it's a lot of time.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.250
- It was the craziest night of filming,

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:38.760
'cause it was a late night, again,

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.090
you have these flickering lights,

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.683
and then here's this guy.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.650
- [Jonathan] Whose blood is that?

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:49.400
- Tom, whatever you've done, it's not you.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.451
He's making you do this.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.561
(vase shatters)

00:00:52.561 --> 00:00:53.394
(Charlie laughs)

00:00:53.394 --> 00:00:54.710
- Had to rehearse that so many times.

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:56.706
Safely, to get the choreography.

00:00:56.706 --> 00:00:59.290
- When I had to hit Michael with the vase,

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:02.500
there was one that's like
a breakaway sugar glass?

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:03.403
Is it sugar glass?
- Yeah, I think so.

00:01:03.403 --> 00:01:05.660
- It's like a breakaway
vase, and then one of them

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:08.040
was a rubber vase, 'cause
we did it multiple times,

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.103
and you have to, like the guy was--

00:01:09.103 --> 00:01:10.333
- One time, you really got him.

00:01:10.333 --> 00:01:12.760
- I know, really, he said
if you hit him harder,

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:14.600
it's gonna hurt less,
that is what he said,

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:15.433
and I was like, really?

00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:17.040
- Very kind to him.
- And Michael was great,

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.200
He was really up for it.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.890
He was like, "No, no, no, I
really want you to hit me."

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.496
And so it's was one of
those where you're like,

00:01:21.496 --> 00:01:23.252
(Charlie inhales), and then--

00:01:23.252 --> 00:01:24.560
- Hit me.
- You just say hit me,

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.973
and I won't, I think I--
- Yeah, you really got him.

00:01:26.973 --> 00:01:30.040
- I got him on the ear, I just
remember his ear being red,

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:30.920
and it was like we'd do a--
- Yeah.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:33.810
Oh my God.
- Smash him on the side,

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:35.170
and then we ran, and it'd be like,

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:36.259
cut, and I'd come back and be like,

00:01:36.259 --> 00:01:37.164
are you all right?
- Are you okay?

00:01:37.164 --> 00:01:37.997
(Charlie chuckles) You all right?

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:38.830
- Good sport.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:39.710
- But he was good.

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:42.381
(vase shattering)
(intense music)

00:01:42.381 --> 00:01:44.560
(Nancy pants)

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:45.393
- Owie.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:49.270
- A lot of it's practical, real makeup.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:50.740
- A lot of it was practical,

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:52.120
all the blood and the sweat.

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:53.540
They made his eyes darker.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:55.130
- Yeah, scary.

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:56.330
He's really tall, too.

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:58.020
Really towers over you.
- Yeah.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:59.124
Go, go, go!

00:01:59.124 --> 00:02:04.114
(Nancy and Jonathan panting)
(intense music)

00:02:04.114 --> 00:02:04.947
- Run!

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:07.745
- Oh, the stairs.
- Oh, yeah.

00:02:07.745 --> 00:02:08.578
The stairs,

00:02:08.578 --> 00:02:09.411
the stairs, the stairs.
- We did this

00:02:09.411 --> 00:02:10.880
about 15 times.
- So many times.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.930
- Obviously, every time you
reset, you're back up and down.

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:15.420
- And, well, there's different
angles of every shot,

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.000
so you're doing it quite a lot,

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.040
it was a very physical--

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:18.873
- It's good.

00:02:18.873 --> 00:02:19.706
- Running day, yeah!
- It helped.

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:23.740
And also, when you reset, you
stop and they change cameras,

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:25.870
you get a maybe 10, 15 minute break.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.240
You reset, but you're not out of breath

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:29.980
and you're not running,
so you do a lot of running

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:32.393
before the take, just on the spot.

00:02:33.732 --> 00:02:37.565
(Nancy and Jonathan panting)

00:02:39.304 --> 00:02:40.830
- Was it Bob doing steady cam?

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.763
- Oh, yeah, that was hard.

00:02:42.763 --> 00:02:44.790
- When we were doing the
steady cam, it was like,

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:48.330
he had to chase us down the
corridor, but backwards,

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:49.510
and then at times--
- And getting the timing

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:51.280
of that was really tricky--
- I think we ran into him

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:52.280
a couple of times.

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:53.830
I slammed the door on him once.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:55.091
It was quite a painful day, yeah.

00:02:55.091 --> 00:02:56.460
- It was, yeah, it was
a lot of physical work.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:57.293
- And your shoes,

00:02:57.293 --> 00:02:58.320
running in high heels.
- Running in those,

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.050
they were these flats, these sling-backs,

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.730
and they're very cute and
they go great with the outfit,

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:04.890
they're really, really hard to run in!

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.390
They're really hard to run in.

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:09.031
- [Jonathan] This way, this way!

00:03:09.031 --> 00:03:12.781
(Nancy and Jonathan panting)

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:15.793
- It was amazing.

00:03:15.793 --> 00:03:18.015
They had this whole empty
hospital to play around in,

00:03:18.015 --> 00:03:20.290
it was quite eerie at times.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:21.970
It's also that crazy
thing about we're running,

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.792
and he's just walking,
but he's right there.

00:03:23.792 --> 00:03:25.610
(intense music)

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:27.908
(Nancy panting)

00:03:27.908 --> 00:03:28.935
- Nancy!

00:03:28.935 --> 00:03:29.802
(intercom buzzes)

00:03:29.802 --> 00:03:30.635
Hello, hello!

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.320
- Here!

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:37.000
- I remember at this point,
our characters are not--

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:37.833
- We're not okay.

00:03:37.833 --> 00:03:38.666
- We're not okay with each other,

00:03:38.666 --> 00:03:41.010
we've argued at this
point, we've fallen out,

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:42.900
things are still not okay with them.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.450
But then, when it matters--

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.040
- Yeah, survival.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:48.360
- When you put your lives at
risk for the other person, so--

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:49.630
- Puts things in perspective,
- Yeah.

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:51.903
- When you get attacked by monsters.

00:03:53.741 --> 00:03:57.028
(door shuts)
(lock clicks)

00:03:57.028 --> 00:03:58.429
- It's ringing!

00:03:58.429 --> 00:04:00.510
- I don't care how good her pie is!

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.877
No, I don't want her in my damn house.

00:04:02.877 --> 00:04:04.410
(Charlie laughs)

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.818
- She was amazing, she was so great.

00:04:06.818 --> 00:04:07.928
- Come on, pick up!

00:04:07.928 --> 00:04:09.257
(lights zapping)

00:04:09.257 --> 00:04:10.090
- Nancy?

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:10.923
- Come on, come on, come on--

00:04:10.923 --> 00:04:14.123
(window shatters)
(Nancy screams)

00:04:14.123 --> 00:04:15.224
- Hi, there.

00:04:15.224 --> 00:04:16.660
- [Charlie] Another breakaway glass?

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:17.897
- [Natalia] You only
have so many of those.

00:04:17.897 --> 00:04:19.254
You really gotta get it right.

00:04:19.254 --> 00:04:20.650
- I think he got glass in his eye.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:22.246
- Yeah, I think he did at one point.

00:04:22.246 --> 00:04:24.408
Still kind of sharp--
- It's not real glass,

00:04:24.408 --> 00:04:25.590
because it breaks away.
- Oh, yeah.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:27.610
- It breaks into small pieces,

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:29.720
and they kind of rub against you.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:32.140
- But they also throw other kind of glass,

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:34.364
that if you step on it,
it gets really slippery.

00:04:34.364 --> 00:04:35.990
- Basically super dangerous.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:38.576
- Super dangerous,
running around like crazy!

00:04:38.576 --> 00:04:41.976
(glass shatters)
(intense music)

00:04:41.976 --> 00:04:42.928
(lock clicks)

00:04:42.928 --> 00:04:43.761
(Nancy gasps)

00:04:43.761 --> 00:04:45.554
(door creaks)

00:04:45.554 --> 00:04:47.403
- I'm here for you, Nancy Drew.

00:04:47.403 --> 00:04:49.903
(Nancy gasps)

00:04:50.786 --> 00:04:52.910
(Jonathan grunts)

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:54.283
- [Nancy] No! (screams)

00:04:54.283 --> 00:04:55.116
(surgical tools crash)

00:04:55.116 --> 00:04:55.949
- We rehearsed this

00:04:55.949 --> 00:04:57.100
quite a lot.
- We rehearsed this

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:57.933
the day before,

00:04:57.933 --> 00:04:58.900
it was a lot of choreography.
- It was a whole day.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.180
- You throw yourself into it a lot,

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:04.300
I kind of wanted to do as
much of it as we could.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:05.550
- Definitely got some bruises

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:06.660
from that day.
- Yeah we got bruises.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.100
Both Jake and Michael were both

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.690
really good at the physical side--

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:13.100
- Yeah, everyone was so
excited for this scene,

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.840
all four of us were like, let's do it.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.128
(surgical tools crash)

00:05:17.128 --> 00:05:18.344
(Jonathan grunts)

00:05:18.344 --> 00:05:19.994
(Jonathan yells)
(body thuds)

00:05:19.994 --> 00:05:20.940
(Jonathan moans)

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:22.600
- Oh that stunt double, poor guy.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:23.663
- There were some
incredible stunt doubles.

00:05:23.663 --> 00:05:25.460
- Some, yeah the doubles were amazing.

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:26.610
- Yeah, they were really good.

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:30.260
- A double who doubles for
you also doubles for Eleven,

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:31.093
earlier this season
- Yeah.

00:05:31.093 --> 00:05:32.983
- Yeah, I was pretty beat at that point.

00:05:35.139 --> 00:05:36.719
(Bruce growls)

00:05:36.719 --> 00:05:37.926
(Jonathan groans)

00:05:37.926 --> 00:05:38.843
- Jonathan!

00:05:39.788 --> 00:05:40.621
(body thuds)
No!

00:05:40.621 --> 00:05:41.750
Oh, brutal.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:42.900
- Yeah, that was me.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.040
- Would you be able to get
up after this in real life?

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:46.121
- I mean, I did.
- That's a lot.

00:05:46.121 --> 00:05:48.982
(Charlie chuckles)

00:05:48.982 --> 00:05:51.268
(Nancy gasping)

00:05:51.268 --> 00:05:52.491
(Jonathan heaves)

00:05:52.491 --> 00:05:53.932
(Nancy gasping)

00:05:53.932 --> 00:05:56.599
(intense music)

00:05:57.622 --> 00:06:00.747
(Bruce yells)
(chair clatters)

00:06:00.747 --> 00:06:03.330
(Bruce groans)

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:05.820
All of the stuff in the hospital,

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:06.780
when the lights are flickering,

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:09.470
after a while, you just feel sick.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:10.730
It looks great, but--
- Yeah.

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:12.250
- Kind of a weird environment to work in.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:13.960
- And sweat, they was always--

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:15.096
- Oh my god, so much.
- Spraying us.

00:06:15.096 --> 00:06:16.490
What was it that they used?

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:18.032
- Sometimes they used glycerine?

00:06:18.032 --> 00:06:19.490
- Glycerine, so it's super sticky.

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:20.460
So you're just--
- Or, like sunscreen.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:22.240
- So all day, you were sticky,

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.810
all around your neck, and it's not--

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:27.352
- Or if it gets in your
eyes, it's not fun.

00:06:27.352 --> 00:06:30.218
(knife clatters)

00:06:30.218 --> 00:06:32.061
(Bruce grunts)

00:06:32.061 --> 00:06:34.302
(Nancy pants)

00:06:34.302 --> 00:06:35.273
- Help!

00:06:35.273 --> 00:06:37.160
Is anyone here?

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:37.993
- Nancy!

00:06:37.993 --> 00:06:40.085
- He has such a Terminator feel about him.

00:06:40.085 --> 00:06:41.585
- Yeah.
- His walk.

00:06:43.037 --> 00:06:45.852
- [Bruce] Nancy!

00:06:45.852 --> 00:06:48.348
(door slams)

00:06:48.348 --> 00:06:50.012
(chair clatters)

00:06:50.012 --> 00:06:51.400
- Where are you going?

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:52.990
- Yeah, it's draining, really.

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:54.380
- It's a lot of energy.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:58.257
- It's such a heightened state,
and you do it so many times,

00:06:58.257 --> 00:07:01.790
but you also have these breaks,
and they're changing angles,

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:02.950
they're moving all the stuff,

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:05.410
so you're really heightened
for a shot a couple times,

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:08.460
then you go sit and then you
be really heightened again.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:11.969
- It's a lot of psyching
yourself up for the moment

00:07:11.969 --> 00:07:14.210
and then you say, dropping off.

00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:16.250
But that also feels really nice,

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:18.900
to come home from a
day's work and feel like

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:21.220
you've put your body through the ringer.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:22.233
I like it.

00:07:22.233 --> 00:07:25.066
(Jonathan grunts)

00:07:27.349 --> 00:07:29.841
(head thuds)

00:07:29.841 --> 00:07:32.344
(metal scrapes)

00:07:32.344 --> 00:07:33.177
- Marco.

00:07:33.177 --> 00:07:36.214
(intense music)

00:07:36.214 --> 00:07:37.200
Marco.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:38.033
- Polo!

00:07:39.041 --> 00:07:43.245
(fire extinguisher thuds)
(Bruce groans)

00:07:43.245 --> 00:07:44.078
(Tom groans)

00:07:44.078 --> 00:07:46.850
Again, a lot of rehearsal, a
lot of going back and forth

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:49.380
between the real fire
extinguisher and a foam one.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:51.286
How does that feel, when
you're holding a foam one?

00:07:51.286 --> 00:07:53.869
(Bruce groans)

00:07:55.641 --> 00:07:57.889
(Tom groans)

00:07:57.889 --> 00:07:58.806
Go to hell!

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:03.020
- I'm just so scared you hurt somebody.

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:05.060
They're like, come on, let's
do it, no, do it for real!

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:06.930
And you're like, okay, ah.

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:07.763
And they're like, just do it!

00:08:07.763 --> 00:08:09.691
It was fun, yeah, it was a lot of fun.

00:08:09.691 --> 00:08:12.358
(intense music)

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:16.670
- [Charlie] So the ones that
you see me stabbing with,

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:19.143
that cut-off scissors,
they have multiple ones.

00:08:19.143 --> 00:08:20.820
- Real ones.
- (laughs) Real ones.

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:21.690
- Fake ones.

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:22.710
- That kinda--
- They're foam.

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:25.330
- It would still putting
them up to his neck.

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:27.830
(eerie music)

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:38.280
- And then his reaction as
well to the whole thing.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.420
How does it feel real?

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:40.570
How do you get yourself in this state?

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:41.560
But when I was doing that,
- You're working.

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:45.600
- His reaction every
time was just so great.

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:48.240
- We hoped you enjoyed this
shot-by-shot breakdown.

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:51.184
Please watch Stranger
Things Season 3 on Netflix.

00:08:51.184 --> 00:08:53.684
(eerie music)

